---
<Layout title={post.title} description={post.description}>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(articleSchema)} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(localBusinessSchema)} />
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 md:px-8 pt-16 pb-24">
    <header class="mb-8">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
        <span class="bg-primary/20 text-primary font-label font-bold text-xs uppercase tracking-widest px-3 py-1 rounded-full">{post.category}</span>
        <time class="font-body text-sm text-secondary">{post.date}</time>
      </div>
      <h1 class="font-headline text-3xl md:text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tighter text-on-surface mb-4">{post.title}</h1>
      <p class="font-body text-lg text-secondary leading-relaxed">{post.description}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
      <section class="mb-12">
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">If you ship product out of Port Klang or KLIA Cargo, you have probably wrestled with ISPM-15 — the international standard requiring all wooden export packaging to be heat-treated and stamped. Miss the stamp, lose the shipment to quarantine. Pay for fumigation, eat the cost. There is a third option that more Malaysian exporters are adopting every quarter: honeycomb cardboard pallets. They are exempt from ISPM-15 entirely, weigh 70% less than wood, and cost less than you might think. Here's the breakdown.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="font-headline text-2xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-6">The ISPM-15 Pain Point</h2>
        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">What ISPM-15 Requires</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">ISPM-15 (International Standards for Phytosanitary Measures) requires all solid wood packaging used in international trade to be heat-treated to 56°C core temperature for 30 minutes, then stamped with the IPPC mark. The intent is preventing pest spread — wood-boring beetles travelling on untreated pallets. Every EU, US, Chinese, Australian, and Japanese port enforces it.</p>

        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">Real Cost Impact</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Per-pallet fumigation runs RM 25-50 in Malaysia. For a 100-pallet sea container that's RM 2,500-5,000 added cost. Then add the documentation overhead — phytosanitary certificates, processor records, customs paperwork. Miss any of it and your shipment sits in quarantine racking up storage fees at the destination port.</p>

        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">Where Honeycomb Side-Steps the Problem</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Honeycomb cardboard pallets are not solid wood. They are paper-based composite. ISPM-15 explicitly exempts paper, plastic, and processed wood-based materials below the threshold. Use them and the entire fumigation/certification chain disappears from your export workflow.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="font-headline text-2xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-6">Weight & Freight Cost Savings</h2>
        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">Air Freight Math</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">A wooden EUR-pallet weighs 20-25kg. The honeycomb equivalent weighs 5-8kg. That's 15-17kg saved per pallet. Air freight to Frankfurt or Los Angeles runs USD 4-7 per kg. Save 15kg per pallet across 50 pallets per shipment, that's USD 3,000-5,250 saved on a single ULD load.</p>

        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">Sea Freight Cubic Optimisation</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">A 40' container priced by gross weight can fit more product if your pallet weight is lower. For Malaysian palm-oil derivative exports and electronics shipments to Europe, the difference is one or two extra pallet positions per container — meaningful margin over the year.</p>

        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">Drayage & Forklift Handling</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Lighter pallets mean lighter forklift demand, faster cycle times in your warehouse, and reduced operator fatigue. Small benefit per pallet, real benefit at scale.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="font-headline text-2xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-6">Where Wood Still Wins</h2>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Honeycomb is not the right answer for every lane. Outdoor yard storage will degrade them quickly — moisture is the enemy. Reusable pool pallets like CHEP make sense for closed-loop operations where the pallet returns. And bulk-density extreme cargo (foundry castings, granite slabs) still needs the load-spreading of timber stringers. Honeycomb wins for one-way export, especially air freight, especially to fumigation-strict markets.</p>
      </section>

      <div class="bg-surface-variant/50 border border-outline-variant/20 rounded-lg p-8 my-12">
        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-6">Honeycomb vs Wooden Pallet Comparison</h3>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
          <div>
            <p class="font-label text-primary font-bold text-sm mb-2">WEIGHT (1100x1100mm)</p>
            <p class="font-body text-on-surface text-sm">Honeycomb 5-8kg | Wood 20-25kg</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-label text-primary font-bold text-sm mb-2">ISPM-15 STATUS</p>
            <p class="font-body text-on-surface text-sm">Honeycomb EXEMPT | Wood required</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-label text-primary font-bold text-sm mb-2">STATIC LOAD</p>
            <p class="font-body text-on-surface text-sm">Honeycomb 500-1500kg | Wood 1500kg+</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-label text-primary font-bold text-sm mb-2">REUSE CYCLES</p>
            <p class="font-body text-on-surface text-sm">Honeycomb 3-5 dry trips | Wood 10+</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="font-headline text-2xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-6">Honeycomb Pallet FAQs</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <details class="group border border-outline-variant/20 rounded-lg p-4">
            <summary class="font-label font-bold text-on-surface cursor-pointer">Are honeycomb pallets accepted for international export?</summary>
            <p class="font-body text-on-surface text-sm mt-3 leading-relaxed">Yes — and exempt from ISPM-15 fumigation. No heat treatment stamp required, no quarantine hold, faster customs clearance.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="group border border-outline-variant/20 rounded-lg p-4">
            <summary class="font-label font-bold text-on-surface cursor-pointer">How much weight can a honeycomb pallet carry?</summary>
            <p class="font-body text-on-surface text-sm mt-3 leading-relaxed">500-1,500kg static and 800kg dynamic for standard. Heavy-duty configs reach 2,000kg+ for machinery exports.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="group border border-outline-variant/20 rounded-lg p-4">
            <summary class="font-label font-bold text-on-surface cursor-pointer">What does it weigh compared to wooden?</summary>
            <p class="font-body text-on-surface text-sm mt-3 leading-relaxed">5-8kg vs 20-25kg for wood. 15kg lighter per pallet — direct air freight savings.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="group border border-outline-variant/20 rounded-lg p-4">
            <summary class="font-label font-bold text-on-surface cursor-pointer">Are honeycomb pallets reusable?</summary>
            <p class="font-body text-on-surface text-sm mt-3 leading-relaxed">3-5 dry indoor round trips, or one-way export. Not for outdoor yard storage.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="group border border-outline-variant/20 rounded-lg p-4">
            <summary class="font-label font-bold text-on-surface cursor-pointer">Are they cost-competitive?</summary>
            <p class="font-body text-on-surface text-sm mt-3 leading-relaxed">Higher per-unit, lower total landed once you factor in fumigation cost and air freight weight savings.</p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12 bg-primary/5 border border-primary/20 rounded-lg p-8">
        <h2 class="font-headline text-2xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">Honeycomb Export Pallets — Made in Balakong</h2>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">If you ship to Europe, North America, China, Japan, or Australia, talk to us about switching your wooden pallets to honeycomb. We make them in standard and custom sizes at our Balakong factory.</p>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface mb-6"><strong>Contact Quinocycle today:</strong></p>
        <ul class="font-body text-on-surface text-sm space-y-2 mb-6">
          <li>📞 <strong>Phone:</strong> +60 16 8916 381 / 03-8962 6381</li>
          <li>📧 <strong>Email:</strong> quinocycle@gmail.com</li>
          <li>📍 <strong>Address:</strong> No.13, Jalan Taming P/1, Taming Jaya, Balakong, Selangor 43300</li>
        </ul>
        <a href={WA_LINK} class="inline-block bg-primary text-on-primary font-label font-bold text-sm px-6 py-3 rounded-lg hover:opacity-90 transition-opacity">💬 Chat on WhatsApp</a>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-8">
        <h2 class="font-headline text-2xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">Conclusion: Re-Run the Export Cost Math</h2>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-4">If you have always used wooden pallets, the assumption may be that they are cheaper. They aren't always — especially once ISPM-15, fumigation, paperwork, and air-freight weight enter the picture. Honeycomb deserves a real evaluation on your top three export lanes.</p>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed">WhatsApp Quinocycle for a side-by-side cost analysis of your current pallet spec versus honeycomb.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
